+- With `X-On-Behalf-Of`, the caller must be a `manager` of the project and the named user must be a member of it (any role); otherwise → 403. Every rule below then applies to the named member, not the caller. For example, a manager acting as a contributor can only change that contributor's own tasks and cannot reassign them.
 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
